[{"id":"VRCE-5-57-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":1,"english":"Having related all, Hanuman, the wind-god's son began again, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ba0a3d71fc5eaad0c95aab59cb43ee6fec2b537dba5c14ca2ebea9febeb63817","compact":"60c1df3e991927906300238ca4726c6729424f6edcd6e522a04b99611438d1a1","nasal":"60c1df3e991927906300238ca4726c6729424f6edcd6e522a04b99611438d1a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":2,"english":"Fruitful is Rāghava's endeavour and Sugrīva's energy, for greatly pleased have I been with Sita's conduct.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.709,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4c0604e3ea4bf2904736fadbefcdb2f0ee36315461fb7e3e87f568de22f450cb","compact":"8aa6313531d5cdf707f57b1b050011dfb3915acaafeb3d0cf5aaa1c33905606d","nasal":"8aa6313531d5cdf707f57b1b050011dfb3915acaafeb3d0cf5aaa1c33905606d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":3,"english":"O heroic monkeys, Sītā has been keeping the life of a highly chaste damsel. She can maintain the animated creation by virtue of her asceticism and burn it with her ire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"38b50bc9f4b5c8ba37e40884aa58546f009bf63045d34688cdf2fb135367a0ba","compact":"ff8337ef8a4b65304af18ee8219322d7b381753129c7b1aca6662809c064363e","nasal":"ff8337ef8a4b65304af18ee8219322d7b381753129c7b1aca6662809c064363e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":4,"english":"Rāvana, the lord of the Rākşasas is also highly advanced in asceticism by virtue whereof he has not been ruined albeit he has touched Sītā's person.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.629,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8725ee7cb54f40cdba9b7316303c12423fc42af05bdaa2930f45dddd7521d661","compact":"6904b068b40af46f3abdd1e51462f2d3d317f9478f94f00c9c014e38e4d85610","nasal":"6904b068b40af46f3abdd1e51462f2d3d317f9478f94f00c9c014e38e4d85610"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":5,"english":"Even the flame of fire cannot do, although touched by the hands, what Janaka's daughter can bring about by her ire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.701,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c1eee6f4b5f9719b56d7f3f3a4e1ede203e0cf056cd156b1a347de1719212f73","compact":"6228a39f79140b5e00e16de5f95211c99a9c771810d3c4218551afebc724f686","nasal":"6228a39f79140b5e00e16de5f95211c99a9c771810d3c4218551afebc724f686"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":6,"english":"(And I beheld there) in the Asoka forest of the vicious-souled Rāvana, at the foot of a ſingśapā tree, the chaste Sītā waiting very poorly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"52ce1313f9d1ce1134534cbfaca76dab4276f79e1af57755834bd047f6858f86","compact":"c195eee11ce18ff13a2088d3bdfca91d8575dcee58421c787b0aa6031e94c3e6","nasal":"c195eee11ce18ff13a2088d3bdfca91d8575dcee58421c787b0aa6031e94c3e6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":7,"english":"She was encircled by the Rākṣasīs, worn out with grief and anxiety and was like to the rays of the Moon shorn of their brilliance being enveloped with clouds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ac6876cd665ab9c9eeb0fa9041fc14b741cbaeaabb92456d991ea3b8172caca9","compact":"1ee5a563818195a4aa0f7cc23c1bc3408c52a6215b8735de93f42eeb0ea99405","nasal":"ea5d266324eb1062514bd848d61071cd505dba7375d8db1956da13a5134b6a59"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":8,"english":"And Vaidehi, having a beautiful waist and devoted to her husband, did not care for Rāvana proud of his prowess and was accordingly confined by him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4c8b9aeb88e7f5127cae81674e8b5b9a372060c1eae19f8c031f0ca1036a6970","compact":"f29c8bf65337d8d2508a528d77fdc2c2b1bf4112b39480ea0c44376f5987baac","nasal":"d588d654e511220da901b0d338458fbb81f63b6e51e5185fca634cd1eb55905c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":9,"english":"And that graceful daughter of the king of Vaidehī was by all means devoted to her lord and had all her thoughts centred in him like to Paulomi (The wife of Indra the lord of the celestials who was confined by the king Nahușa) devoted to her lord Purandara.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.649,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a64c9dff56b7609d10ac5536e8d86097403a6f71d9d2f6e78f9567b5ae8d69e9","compact":"23d475d16f26eb46061926b73fe6c6f21a57db44b805f7e3b70de9e01a73b7e0","nasal":"23d475d16f26eb46061926b73fe6c6f21a57db44b805f7e3b70de9e01a73b7e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":10,"english":"And I saw her in that garden, wearing a single piece of cloth soiled with dirt, surrounded by the Rākşasīs and remonstrated with now and then by those ugly demons. Having a single braid of hair, poorly, engaged in thoughts touching her lord, she was lying on the earth shorn of all grace like to a lotus on the appearance of the winter. She had not the least attachment for Rāvana and was resolved upon putting an end to her existence.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.407,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-59-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5057010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54d2585c3f7e4c1fa999e39dd3805dac6b7d919e735b354828ecd3b4c1c210c9","compact":"9690b6fc7783ebd999739cdbaa45f43f866510d665e5971a268c08bd9c67ec6d","nasal":"a259a47c111d453520439d3dc962e67da2cb0f1e7588b6277292bf13bf72e938"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-57-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":57,"verse":11,"english":"And I saw her in that garden, wearing a single piece of cloth soiled with dirt, surrounded by the Rākşasīs and remonstrated with now and then by those ugly demons. Having a single braid of hair, poorly, engaged in thoughts touching her lord, she was lying on the earth shorn of all grace like to a lotus on the appearance of the winter. She had not the least attachment for Rāvana and was resolved upon putting an end to her existence.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","c